Pippa patch for llama.cpp b11503 (03aa006acb547549162a00dddeab3d3b38ebf7b2).

Why: the K2 Horizon parser (common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp) only accepts the think end tag of the requested
reasoning_effort (</ifm|think_faster> for low, </ifm|think_fast> for medium). K2 often writes
<ifm|think>...</ifm|think> after tool results, so the tool calls that follow end up in reasoning_content and
Pi's turn ends empty. With this patch every effort's end tag closes the reasoning block.
Measured: official low 24/30 OK, medium 0/20; patched low 19/20 with zero leaks.
Same change as the regression-tested version on llama.cpp master (scratch branch, not submitted).

Goes away once upstream accepts it (see docs/rebuild/llama-cpp-k2-pr.md); then delete this file and the
"patches" entry in llama-release.json.

Applied by scripts/build-app.sh with `patch -p1`.

diff --git a/common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp b/common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp
--- a/common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp
+++ b/common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,13 @@ common_chat_params common_chat_params_init_k2_horizon(const common_chat_template
     const std::string ARG_VAL_END   = "</ifm|arg_value>";
 
     data.thinking_start_tag = THINK_START;
+    // The model may close with another effort's tag (often </ifm|think> after tool results), keep THINK_END first for the reasoning budget
     data.thinking_end_tags  = { THINK_END };
+    for (const std::string tag : { "</ifm|think>", "</ifm|think_fast>", "</ifm|think_faster>" }) {
+        if (tag != THINK_END) {
+            data.thinking_end_tags.push_back(tag);
+        }
+    }
 
     data.preserved_tokens = data.thinking_end_tags;
     data.preserved_tokens.insert(data.preserved_tokens.end(), {
